
IBM Integration Bus (IIB) / ACE me DFDL ka use hota hai to define non-XML data structures (text, binary, COBOL, etc.).
Agar tumhare paas ek COBOL copybook hai (jo ek fixed data format describe karti hai), to tum ise DFDL schema me convert kar sakte ho using the COBOL importer wizard.

Isse fayda ye hota hai:

Tumhe manually DFDL likhne ki zarurat nahi.

COBOL data ko IIB message flow me as structured message treat kar sakte ho.

Reusability aur consistency maintain hoti hai.



---

⚙️ Before You Begin

🧩 Linux ke liye Requirement:

Agar tum Linux system par ho, to COBOL importer ko kuch 32-bit system libraries chahiye hoti hain.
Ye libraries kuch distributions me default install nahi hoti, jaise:

Red Hat Enterprise Linux V6 (64-bit)

Ubuntu 10.4+ (32-bit aur 64-bit)


👉 IBM ne ek page diya hai jahan bataya gaya hai ki kaunsi libraries install karni hain:
https://www.ibm.com/support/docview.wss?uid=swg21512074


---

🧾 About This Task

COBOL importer wizard do main cheezein karta hai:

1. Importing a COBOL copybook or program

Ye copybook ek structure define karti hai — jaise record layouts, field names, field types, etc.

❗ Important rules:

Copybook me COBOL reserved keywords field names ke liye use nahi hone chahiye.

File ka name 60 characters se zyada nahi hona chahiye, warna importer fail hoga with error:
👉 IWAA0652E: File name cannot be longer than 60 characters




2. Importing or replacing IBM-supplied DFDL COBOL format schema

Matlab tum IBM ke prebuilt COBOL DFDL base format ko apne data structure ke sath use kar sakte ho ya replace kar sakte ho.





---

🪄 Procedure (Steps to Create DFDL from COBOL)

1. Open IIB Toolkit


2. Click:
File > New > Other > Message Model


3. Select: COBOL


4. Follow the wizard:

Select your COBOL copybook file (.cpy)

Configure DFDL namespace, element names, and encoding

Finish the wizard




👉 IIB automatically DFDL schema file generate karega jisse tum message parsing me use kar sakte ho.



